---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
		<title>Hunt Templates - Untamed GM Guide</title>
		<meta name="description" content="Quick hunt templates for Untamed GMs: alternative mission frameworks beyond track and slay, including harvest, relocate, rescue, population control, ecology disruption, and bait and observe." />
	</head>
	<body>
		<nav class="nav">
			<div class="container">
				<a href="/" class="logo">UNTAMED</a>
				<div class="nav-links">
					<a href="/rules">Rules</a>
					<a href="/quick-reference">Quick Reference</a>
					<a href="/character">Characters</a>
					<a href="/bestiary">Bestiary</a>
					<a href="/gm-guide" class="active">GM Guide</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</nav>

		<main>
			<div class="container">
				<div class="breadcrumb">
					<a href="/gm-guide">← Back to GM Guide</a>
				</div>

				<header class="page-header">
					<h1>Hunt Templates</h1>
					<p class="subtitle">Not every mission has to be "find it and kill it."</p>
				</header>

				<article class="content">
					<!-- INTRO -->
					<section class="major-section">
						<h2 class="section-title">VII. Tools for GM Creativity</h2>

						<div class="rule-section highlight">
							<h3 class="phase-heading">🧩 Quick Hunt Templates</h3>
							<p>Not every mission has to be "find it and kill it."</p>
							<p>Mixing up objectives keeps players thinking, planning, and adapting.</p>
							<p>Use these templates to quickly set up a hunt:</p>
						</div>
					</section>

					<!-- TEMPLATES -->
					<section class="major-section">
						<div class="template-card">
							<h2>🎯 "Track and Slay"</h2>
							<p class="template-flavor">Classic hunt format: Locate a monster, study it, and eliminate it before it migrates or causes further damage.</p>
							<p><strong>Objective:</strong> Defeat the target monster.</p>
							<p><strong>Variations:</strong> Kill it before it reaches a certain sector. Kill it before nightfall.</p>
							<p><strong>Example:</strong></p>
							<blockquote class="example">"A Kragal has been attacking supply caravans along the cliffside routes. Hunt it down before it disrupts trade routes further."</blockquote>
						</div>

						<div class="template-card">
							<h2>🧵 "Harvest Rare Material"</h2>
							<p class="template-flavor">Sometimes the goal isn't to kill — it's to collect valuable materials without causing unnecessary damage.</p>
							<p><strong>Objective:</strong> Break a specific part (horn, tail, etc.) or steal rare resources (e.g., from nests or territories).</p>
							<p><strong>Variations:</strong> Damage-only mission; monster survives if properly harvested.</p>
							<p><strong>Example:</strong></p>
							<blockquote class="example">"A Tanuza nest was spotted high in the canopy — retrieve its rare Glider Membranes without killing the creature if possible."</blockquote>
						</div>

						<div class="template-card">
							<h2>⚠️ "Relocate Threat"</h2>
							<p class="template-flavor">The creature is too valuable, sacred, or critical to the ecosystem to kill. Instead, it must be relocated — alive.</p>
							<p><strong>Objective:</strong> Subdue the monster without lethal force and drive or trap it into a designated zone.</p>
							<p><strong>Variations:</strong> Special traps, baiting, or terrain manipulation missions.</p>
							<p><strong>Example:</strong></p>
							<blockquote class="example">"An elder Urmine has wandered too close to the village's outskirts. Trap it or bait it back toward the wilds without causing permanent harm."</blockquote>
						</div>

						<div class="template-card">
							<h2>🚑 "Rescue Mission"</h2>
							<p class="template-flavor">A hunter, researcher, or NPC has gone missing in dangerous territory — and the clock is ticking.</p>
							<p><strong>Objective:</strong> Find and escort the target safely out.</p>
							<p><strong>Variations:</strong> Target may be injured and unable to fight. Random event rolls increase while escorting.</p>
							<p><strong>Example:</strong></p>
							<blockquote class="example">"A herbalist went missing while gathering Thunderfruit in the Verdant Hollow. Track her down before nightfall, and beware territorial Gorrhul."</blockquote>
						</div>

						<div class="template-card">
							<h2>🐺 "Population Control"</h2>
							<p class="template-flavor">Certain creatures have overpopulated an area, threatening balance or critical food sources.</p>
							<p><strong>Objective:</strong> Reduce numbers to a manageable level.</p>
							<p><strong>Variations:</strong> Target Alpha leaders to cause dispersal instead of full extermination.</p>
							<p><strong>Example:</strong></p>
							<blockquote class="example">"The Vorvarg packs have grown too bold, raiding village stores nightly. Cull their numbers — or slay their Alpha to scatter the pack."</blockquote>
						</div>

						<div class="template-card">
							<h2>🌍 "Ecology Disruption"</h2>
							<p class="template-flavor">A dangerous shift in the environment must be stopped — or at least delayed.</p>
							<p><strong>Objective:</strong> Interfere with a monster migration, a blooming event, or territorial expansions.</p>
							<p><strong>Variations:</strong> Set controlled fires, destroy pollen nests, defeat Apex monsters.</p>
							<p><strong>Example:</strong></p>
							<blockquote class="example">"Signs of an Apex Stagmir awakening have appeared. Disrupt the bioluminescent blooms before they trigger a migration."</blockquote>
						</div>

						<div class="template-card">
							<h2>🐾 "Bait and Observe"</h2>
							<p class="template-flavor">Scientists, sages, or hunters need information — not a kill. Sometimes, the mission is about watching and learning.</p>
							<p><strong>Objective:</strong> Track the monster, record behavior, and survive encounters.</p>
							<p><strong>Variations:</strong> May involve deploying scent markers, baiting areas, or surviving multiple close calls.</p>
							<p><strong>Example:</strong></p>
							<blockquote class="example">"The Guild needs behavioral data on the Earule's aerial hunts. Trail the beast and observe without engaging unless absolutely necessary."</blockquote>
						</div>
					</section>

					<!-- MIXERS -->
					<section class="major-section">
						<h2 class="section-title">🎯 Bonus: Mini-Hunt Challenge Mixers</h2>
						<div class="rule-section">
							<p>You can combine templates for richer hunts:</p>
							<ul>
								<li><strong>Track and Slay + Harvest Rare Material</strong> (Kill it and break specific parts!)</li>
								<li><strong>Rescue Mission + Ecology Disruption</strong> (Rescue someone caught during an environmental collapse!)</li>
								<li><strong>Relocate Threat + Bait and Observe</strong> (Study the beast's path before baiting it into a trap!)</li>
							</ul>
						</div>
					</section>

					<!-- FINAL ADVICE -->
					<section class="major-section">
						<h2 class="section-title">🧠 Final GM Advice</h2>
						<div class="rule-section highlight">
							<ul class="check-list">
								<li>Change up goals regularly!</li>
								<li>Use terrain and random events to push players to rethink their tactics.</li>
								<li>Let success or failure ripple into the world (e.g., population booms, damaged villages, hero celebrations).</li>
							</ul>
						</div>
					</section>
				</article>
			</div>

			<footer class="footer">
				<div class="container">
					<p>
						This is the Playtest version. Some monster art is AI-generated; the final version will use original artist drawings.
					</p>
					<p class="footer-creed">The wild does not forgive. But it rewards those who respect the hunt.</p>
				</div>
			</footer>
		</main>

		<style>
			* {
				margin: 0;
				padding: 0;
				box-sizing: border-box;
			}

			:root {
				--forest-dark: #1a2e1a;
				--forest-green: #2d5016;
				--moss-green: #4a7c2f;
				--leaf-green: #6b9d3a;
				--amber: #d4a257;
				--earth-brown: #5c4033;
				--cream: #f5f1e8;
				--text-light: #e8e4d8;
			}

			body {
				font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, sans-serif;
				background: var(--forest-dark);
				color: var(--text-light);
				line-height: 1.7;
				min-height: 100vh;
			}

			.container {
				max-width: 1000px;
				margin: 0 auto;
				padding: 0 2rem;
			}

			/* Navigation */
			.nav {
				background: var(--forest-green);
				border-bottom: 2px solid var(--amber);
				padding: 1rem 0;
				position: sticky;
				top: 0;
				z-index: 100;
			}

			.nav .container {
				display: flex;
				justify-content: space-between;
				align-items: center;
				max-width: 1200px;
			}

			.logo {
				font-size: 1.5rem;
				font-weight: 900;
				color: var(--amber);
				text-decoration: none;
				letter-spacing: 0.2rem;
			}

			.nav-links {
				display: flex;
				gap: 2rem;
			}

			.nav-links a {
				color: var(--cream);
				text-decoration: none;
				font-weight: 500;
				transition: color 0.3s;
			}

			.nav-links a:hover,
			.nav-links a.active {
				color: var(--amber);
			}

			/* Breadcrumb */
			.breadcrumb {
				padding: 2rem 0 1rem;
			}

			.breadcrumb a {
				color: var(--leaf-green);
				text-decoration: none;
				font-weight: 500;
			}

			.breadcrumb a:hover {
				color: var(--amber);
			}

			/* Page Header */
			.page-header {
				padding: 2rem 0 2rem;
				text-align: center;
				border-bottom: 2px solid var(--amber);
				margin-bottom: 2rem;
			}

			.page-header h1 {
				font-size: 3rem;
				color: var(--amber);
				margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
			}

			.subtitle {
				font-size: 1.25rem;
				color: var(--leaf-green);
				font-style: italic;
			}

			/* Content */
			.content {
				padding-bottom: 4rem;
			}

			/* Major Sections */
			.major-section {
				margin-bottom: 4rem;
				scroll-margin-top: 100px;
			}

			.section-title {
				font-size: 2.2rem;
				color: var(--amber);
				margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
				padding-bottom: 1rem;
				border-bottom: 3px solid var(--amber);
			}

			/* Rule Sections */
			.rule-section {
				background: var(--forest-green);
				padding: 1.5rem;
				border-radius: 8px;
				margin: 1.5rem 0;
				border: 2px solid var(--earth-brown);
			}

			.rule-section.highlight {
				border-color: var(--amber);
				background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--forest-green) 0%, var(--moss-green) 100%);
			}

			.phase-heading {
				color: var(--amber);
				font-size: 1.3rem;
				margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
				letter-spacing: 0.03rem;
			}

			.rule-section p {
				color: var(--text-light);
				margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
			}

			.rule-section ul {
				margin-left: 1.5rem;
				margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
			}

			.rule-section li {
				margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
				color: var(--text-light);
			}

			/* Template Cards */
			.template-card {
				background: var(--forest-green);
				padding: 2rem;
				border-radius: 10px;
				margin: 1.5rem 0;
				border: 2px solid var(--earth-brown);
				border-left: 6px solid var(--amber);
				transition: border-color 0.3s ease, transform 0.3s ease;
			}

			.template-card:hover {
				border-color: var(--amber);
				transform: translateY(-2px);
			}

			.template-card h2 {
				color: var(--amber);
				font-size: 1.65rem;
				margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
				letter-spacing: 0.02rem;
			}

			.template-card p {
				color: var(--text-light);
				margin-bottom: 0.65rem;
			}

			.template-card .template-flavor {
				font-style: italic;
				color: var(--cream);
				margin-bottom: 1rem;
			}

			.template-card strong {
				color: var(--leaf-green);
			}

			/* Blockquote / Example */
			blockquote.example {
				background: var(--forest-dark);
				border-left: 4px solid var(--amber);
				padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
				margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
				border-radius: 6px;
				font-style: italic;
				color: var(--cream);
				font-size: 1.05rem;
			}

			/* Check List */
			.check-list {
				list-style: none;
				margin-left: 0 !important;
				padding-left: 0;
			}

			.check-list li {
				position: relative;
				padding-left: 2rem;
				margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
				color: var(--text-light);
				font-size: 1.05rem;
			}

			.check-list li::before {
				content: "✅";
				position: absolute;
				left: 0;
				top: 0;
			}

			/* Footer */
			.footer {
				padding: 3rem 0;
				background: var(--forest-dark);
				border-top: 3px solid var(--earth-brown);
				text-align: center;
				color: var(--moss-green);
			}

			.footer p {
				font-size: 0.95rem;
				margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
			}

			.footer-creed {
				font-style: italic;
				color: var(--leaf-green);
				margin-top: 1rem;
			}

			/* Responsive */
			@media (max-width: 768px) {
				.nav .container {
					flex-direction: column;
					gap: 1rem;
				}

				.nav-links {
					gap: 1rem;
					flex-wrap: wrap;
					justify-content: center;
				}

				.page-header h1 {
					font-size: 2rem;
				}

				.section-title {
					font-size: 1.6rem;
				}

				.template-card {
					padding: 1.5rem;
				}

				.template-card h2 {
					font-size: 1.4rem;
				}

				.rule-section {
					padding: 1.25rem;
				}
			}
		</style>
	</body>
</html>
